{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774456865,"nonce":"hy2WvgVX5uSL/Pd7QTdOD8aTN1k=","title":"Feature: SDK agent question-asking via modal forms in the web UI","message":"SDK agents should be able to ask the user questions during a chat by triggering modal forms and other rich UI elements in the Mandible web app. This goes beyond the current permission dialog (which is approve/deny only) to support:\n\n- Free-text questions (\"What should the branch be named?\")\n- Multiple-choice selection (\"Which of these approaches do you prefer?\")\n- Confirmation dialogs (\"This will delete 3 files. Proceed?\")\n- Multi-field forms (e.g., \"Provide a title, description, and priority for this issue\")\n- File/path pickers\n- Dropdown selectors populated from Mandible data (repos, presets, issues)\n\nThe SDK agent would emit a structured \"question\" event with the form schema. The UI renders the appropriate form, collects the response, and sends it back to the agent as a tool result. The agent blocks until the user responds.\n\nThis is straightforward with the existing SDK backend infrastructure — we already have the permission dialog pattern (agent emits request, UI renders, user responds, result sent back). This generalizes that pattern from binary approve/deny to arbitrary form inputs.\n\nCould also support non-blocking questions (agent continues working, user responds later) and question queuing (multiple questions batched into one form).","files":null}]}